cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Structure Without Reading: a reproducible structural analysis of the rongorongo corpus"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rochala
    given-names: Piotr
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-07
repository-code: "https://github.com/rochal/rongorongo"
url: "https://github.com/rochal/rongorongo"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - rongorongo
  - Easter Island
  - Rapa Nui
  - undeciphered scripts
  - corpus analysis
  - digital humanities
abstract: >-
  Scripts, generated tables and a working report analysing the rongorongo
  corpus of Easter Island for structure without assigning meaning to any
  sign. Uses the CEIPP numerical transliteration of Barthel's corpus,
  Barthel's sign catalogue and tracings, the retouched photographs of the
  tablets, Thomson's 1891 recitations, Metraux's 1940 texts, Jaussen's 1893
  record of Metoro's chanted readings, and public-domain Maori and Tahitian
  texts as related-language models. Covers parallel passages and text
  families, delimited lists, alternating series, an affix test for the
  stroke signs, allograph mining and a context test for rare signs, sign
  inventories against Polynesian words and syllables at matched sample
  size, shape similarity, genre clustering, sequence entropy, collocations,
  compound decomposition, the Santiago Staff, the Mamari calendar under
  three counting rules, the consistency of Metoro's readings, a statistical
  decipherment attempt with positive controls and a text-length bound, the
  registration of the tracings to the photographs with hand-corrected boxes
  as ground truth, and a log of places where carving, tracing and
  transliteration disagree; each result with a control or a shuffled null,
  and a fresh-clone reproduction check.
